# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny by default.
#
# Broad denials first, then narrow re-inclusions ONLY for fixture directories
# that CI verifies are synthetic. Do not add re-inclusions below without a
# corresponding check in tools/scan_pii.py.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Everything the user feeds in, and everything derived from it.
# Nothing under these paths can be re-included: git will not descend into an
# excluded directory, which is exactly the property we want here.
/data/
/data.bak-*/
/output/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Common report formats anywhere outside fixtures. Every suffix here is one a
# right-to-know response actually arrives as, and every one of them is a format
# tools/scan_pii.py cannot read — so if one is ever committed, no rule in the
# scanner gets a look at it. Denying them outright is the only check that works.
*.pdf
*.zip
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.ods
*.doc
*.docx
*.eml
*.mbox
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Screen captures of a receipt viewer are a response format too, as of the H Mart
# second reply, and they are the worst case the list has: `tools/scan_pii.py`
# skips image suffixes outright (SKIP_SUFFIXES), gitleaks matches no secret
# pattern in them, and a capture is tens of KB so the large-file hook never
# fires. A real one committed outside a fixtures directory would pass every gate
# this repo has. The re-inclusions below are the three directories that hold
# images the project actually ships.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# The one re-inclusion, and the reason it is safe: `make fixtures-check` (CI)
# regenerates every file in these directories from a fixed seed and fails on any
# file it did not produce, so nothing lands here that a generator did not write.
# tests/fixtures/** used to be re-included alongside this one and was covered by
# no such check — an exemption with nothing behind it, which is the shape of the
# accident this file exists to prevent. Do not re-add a re-inclusion without a
# corresponding check in tools/make_fixtures.py.
!src/**/fixtures/**

# Images the project ships, none of which is a response. `resources/` holds the
# brand sources, `frontend/public/` the built icons the app serves, and
# `docs/screenshots/` the README captures — which `tools/make_screenshots.py`
# takes from a scratch container it builds itself, never from ./data.
!resources/**
!frontend/public/**
!docs/screenshots/**

# The PII scanner's literal denylist is itself a PII file.
tools/denylist.txt

# gstack tool output: QA reports, design audits, screenshots. Artifacts about
# the project, not part of it, and they would otherwise land as untracked files
# in a repo whose whole posture is that stray files are a hazard.
/.gstack/

# tests/container/test_layout.py bind-mounts this into a real container as
# /data, so it grows the same db/ and incoming/ pair that data/ has — an
# ingested report and a SQLite database, in the repo root, created by a test
# run. The fixture it ingests is synthetic, but the directory is shaped exactly
# like the one this file exists to keep out, and it was previously left
# untracked and un-ignored where `git add .` would take it.
/.pytest-layout-data/

# `make screenshots` mounts this into a throwaway container as /data. Same shape
# as data/, same reason to keep it out. Removed on success; this covers a crash.
/.screenshot-data/

# Local overrides
*.local.*
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ordinary build and tooling noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

node_modules/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/dist/

# Built UI. Reproducible from frontend/ via the Docker build; committing a
# minified bundle would put unreviewable generated code in every diff.
/src/unbagged/static/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
